			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1011415">
									

<p>I strongly approve.</p>
<p>I love that it looks like an ongoing document rather than the results of long term research. The unanswered questions offered by the second and third notes lead to far more interesting places in the mind of the reader than anything you could possibly write. Now that you've gotten that far, though, temptation to ruin the delicate balance you've achieved will come in the form of comments asking for clarification.</p>
<p>My advice: <em>ignore <strong>anything</strong> anyone tells you to add to this page.</em> It's excellent as-is. Like I said, at this point anything you add can only detract from the spirit of the piece.</p>
<p>(Ignore sophos. I usually do. It's not boring.)</p>
<p>Do consider italicizing the researcher's notes, though. Addenda are in italics throughout the site, and there's no harm in fitting in.</p>

